{"id":"a07bf08781c5a82a","group":"58","path":"58/batch06/58-df-spectral-theorem.md","title":"Spectral Theorem","display":"df-spectral-theorem — Spectral Theorem","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-spectral-theorem","aliases":["58-df-spectral-theorem","Spectral Theorem"],"display":"df-spectral-theorem — Spectral Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-spectral-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-spectral-theorem</span><span>Spectral Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-spectral-theorem — Spectral Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"6da70a87682c611a\" href=\"?note=6da70a87682c611a\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md\">../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"71f1954115db03be\" href=\"?note=71f1954115db03be\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md\">../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,E,H\\in V\">\\(A,E,H\\in V\\)</span> (parameters)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\\)</span> (self-adjoint predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"6da70a87682c611a\" href=\"?note=6da70a87682c611a\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md\">../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PVM}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{PVM}_S\\)</span> (projection-valued-measure predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"71f1954115db03be\" href=\"?note=71f1954115db03be\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md\">../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SpectralResolution}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{SpectralResolution}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (spectral-resolution relation defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}spectral\\text{-}theorem}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SpectralResolution}_S(A,E,H)\\leftrightarrow\n\\left(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(A,H)\\land\n\\mathrm{PVM}_S(E,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R),H)\\land\nA=\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda\\,dE(\\lambda)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}spectral\\text{-}theorem}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SpectralResolution}_S(A,E,H)\\leftrightarrow\n\\left(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(A,H)\\land\n\\mathrm{PVM}_S(E,\\mathbb R,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb R),H)\\land\nA=\\int_{\\mathbb R}\\lambda\\,dE(\\lambda)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}spectral\\text{-}theorem}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{SpectralResolution}(A,E)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SpectralResolution}_S(A,E,H)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}spectral\\text{-}theorem}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{SpectralResolution}(A,E)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{SpectralResolution}_S(A,E,H)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>谱定理断言每个自伴算子存在唯一满足该关系的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\">\\(E\\)</span>；存在唯一性与谱/范数结论是定理，不是定义。</li>\n<li>Multiplication operator form: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A \\cong M_f\">\\(A \\cong M_f\\)</span> on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^2(\\mu)\">\\(L^2(\\mu)\\)</span></li>\n<li>Functional calculus: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f(A) = \\int f(\\lambda) dE_\\lambda\">\\(f(A) = \\int f(\\lambda) dE_\\lambda\\)</span></li>\n<li>Borel functional calculus: bounded/normal operators</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reed and Simon, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Teschl, Mathematical Methods in Quantum Mechanics</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"6da70a87682c611a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md","status":"resolved","id":"71f1954115db03be","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"6da70a87682c611a","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S$ (self-adjoint predicate, see [[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md","status":"resolved","id":"71f1954115db03be","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{PVM}_S$ (projection-valued-measure predicate, see [[../batch12/58-df-projection-valued.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A,E,H\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PVM}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SpectralResolution}_S\\subse